==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|hƿæt}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*hwat}}, from {{inh|ang|ine-pro|*kʷos}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kʷod}}. Cognates include {{cog|ofs|hwet}} ({{cog|fy|wat}}), {{cog|osx|hwat}} ({{cog|nds|wat}}), {{cog|nl|wat}}, {{cog|goh|hwaz}} ({{cog|de|was}}), {{cog|non|hvat}} ({{cog|da|hvad}}, {{cog|sv|vad}}), {{cog|got|𐍈𐌰}}. The Indo-European root also led to the {{cog|la|quod}}, {{cog|lt|kàd}}, and {{cog|ga|cad}}.

